 "_about": "SLE snow guns (a fictional snowmaking maker; code name SLE, owner 2026-09-29). Our own builds; every dimension from the owner's reference model, measured locally and never named. Millimetres. Stick gun frame, as measured: on the post's axis, w 0 at the reference's snow line, u the way the lance leans, v along the pivot pin, w up; the asset's origin is on the post's axis at grade (w = grade). Lance parts are placed along the lance: s along its axis, c across it (in the u-w plane, + toward its upper side), v sideways; a point is s * axis + (c0 + c) * across.",
 "_adjust": [
  "symmetric about the centre plane v = 0 (the reference's head parts sit up to 4 mm off it)",
  "the sleeve's web drops 3.7 mm to sit under the lance channel rather than through it",
  "the base mast: the reference's 5 ft post stands on the ground, the pivot 1150 mm above grade and 449 mm of post below it (the reference set it almost wholly below its snow line; the owner's photos show the lance pinned on a mast's top), so the stay's clevis on the mast shows and is built",
  "the ground gun's head is sized from the owner's close-up photos of a real unit (the reference drew it small), and its tripod follows those photos; the stick gun's head takes the same dimensions (the owner: very similar): the fan block, a 305 mm barrel and the 74 mm cap, on the tower's own Y block",
  "lance length procedural: 10, 20 or 30 ft of pipe (the reference is 20 ft); the head rides on the pipe's end, the channel stops 1524 mm (5 ft) short of it"
 ],
